  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namosi Hydropower Generation Feasibility Study - Fiji - Energy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AIFFP is financing a feasibility study regarding potential development of three relatively small run-of-river hydropower plants in Namosi catchment area. The proposed hydropower schemes are on the Wainikoroiluva, Wainikovu, and Waivaka rivers.  Hydropower development in the Namosi area is part of the Government of Fiji&#x2019;s commitment to address climate change &amp; its target of 100% renewable energy by 2036.  Energy Fiji Limited (EFL) is required to implement the Government&#x2019;s climate change and renewable objective and vision. The Namosi Hydropower Project (Namosi HP) is a potential renewable energy project that could help EFL to meet this objective. The Feasibility Study&#x2019;s objective is to assess if it is viable to develop the hydropower potential in the Namosi area into operational hydroelectric power stations, taking into account a range of technical, environmental and social considerations, in line with best international practices and the laws and regulations of Fiji.</narrative>
  </description>
